    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">EMP301 · Chapter 5 · Session 24</span>\n<h2>Session 24 — Chapter 5: Lexeme Formation: Further Afield</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14440 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">EMP301 · Chương 5 · Buổi 24</span>\n<h2>Buổi 24 — Chapter 5: Lexeme Formation: Further Afield</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14440 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1,3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I T U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">6</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1,3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I T U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">6</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 5: Lexeme Formation: Further Afield<br>Templatic Morphology<br>Subtractive processes</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Course book: Introducing Morphology<br>Chapter 5 (pages 98-100)<br>Online resources</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>Preview the lesson<br>Participate in class discussions and activities<br>Complete tasks before, during, and after the lesson</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>📑 School slides — EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 (6 slides)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">matched by the session number in the deck name. File: EMP301_SESSION 24_Chapter 5.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>📑 Slide của trường — EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 (6 slide)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">ghép theo số buổi ghi trong tên deck. Tệp: EMP301_SESSION 24_Chapter 5.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d24/001.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 1: CHAPTER 5.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 1/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>CHAPTER 5.<br>Lexeme Formation: Further Afield</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d24/002.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 2: 5.6 Templatic Morphology\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 2/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>5.6 Templatic Morphology﻿﻿<br>﻿Each word has a different pattern of vowels and consonants, and each expresses a slightly different concept. What we find in Arabic is called templatic morphology or root and pattern morphology.<br>﻿Each of these template patterns is called a binyan, a term which comes from traditional Hebrew grammar.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d24/003.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 3: 5.6 Templatic Morphology\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 3/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>5.6 Templatic Morphology</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d24/004.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 4: 5.7 Subtractive Processes\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 4/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>5.7 Subtractive Processes﻿﻿<br>﻿Not all lexeme formation is additive, however. There are some languages that have processes that we might call subtractive in the sense that the derived lexeme consists of a base from which something has been removed.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d24/005.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 5: 5.7 Subtractive Processes\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 5/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>5.7 Subtractive Processes﻿﻿<br>﻿It’s common in English to form nicknames (hypocoristics, if you want the technical term!) by subtracting part of the full name.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d24/006.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 6: THANK YOU!\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 SESSION 24 Chapter 5 · slide 6/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>THANK YOU!</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
