    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">EMP301 · Chapter 8 · Session 39</span>\n<h2>Session 39 — Chapter 8: Words and Sentences: The Interface between Morphology and Syntax</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14440 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">EMP301 · Chương 8 · Buổi 39</span>\n<h2>Buổi 39 — Chapter 8: Words and Sentences: The Interface between Morphology and Syntax</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14440 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1,6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I T U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">7</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO1,6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I T U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">7</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 8: Words and Sentences: The Interface between Morphology and Syntax<br>Argument Structure and Morphology (cont)</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Course book: Introducing Morphology<br>Chapter 8 (pages 169-171)<br>Online resources</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>Preview the lesson<br>Participate in class discussions and activities<br>Complete tasks before, during, and after the lesson</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>📑 School slides — EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 (7 slides)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">matched by the session number in the deck name. File: EMP301_Session 39_Chapter 8.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>📑 Slide của trường — EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 (7 slide)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">ghép theo số buổi ghi trong tên deck. Tệp: EMP301_Session 39_Chapter 8.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d39/001.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 1: CHAPTER 8.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 1/7</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>CHAPTER 8.<br>Words and Sentences: The Interface between Morphology and Syntax<br>Session 39</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d39/002.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 2: 8.2.2 Causative and Applicative (P.168)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 2/7</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>8.2.2 Causative and Applicative (P.168)<br>Passive and anti-passive morphology signal a reduction in the number of arguments that a verb has.<br>There are other sorts of morphology that signal that arguments have been added to a verb.<br>Causatives signal the addition of a new subject argument, which semantically is the causer of the action.<br>If the verb has only 01 argument to begin with, the causative sentence has 02,<br>If it has 02 to begin with, the causative sentence has 03 arguments.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d39/003.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 3: 8.2.2 Causative and Applicative (P.168)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 3/7</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>8.2.2 Causative and Applicative (P.168)<br>In (a), the verb ‘boil’ has only one argument, its patient/theme.<br>In (b), along with the causative morpheme -(i)sh, an external causer argument is added as the subject of the sentence.<br>Similarly, in (a), the verb ‘cook’ has<br>two arguments, an agent (Halima) and a patient (‘food’); the agent is the subject of the sentence.<br>When the causative suffix -(i)sh is added, a third argument (Juma) is added and it becomes the subject.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d39/004.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 4: 8.2.2 Causative and Applicative (P.168)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 4/7</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>8.2.2 Causative and Applicative (P.168)<br>Applicative morphology, like causative morphology, signals the addition of an argument to the valency of a verb. But the add ed argument is an object, rather than a subject. We can again use Swahili for our example:<br>The suffix -i signals that a second object (Juma) has been added to the verb.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d39/005.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 5: 8.2.3 Noun Incorporation (p.171)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 5/7</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>8.2.3 Noun Incorporation (p.171)<br>﻿Sentences (11a) and (11b) mean precisely the same thing in Mapudungun. In (11a), the direct object ‘the cows’ is an independent noun phrase in the sentence, but in (11b), it forms a single compound-like word with the verb root ‘seek’. This sort of structure – where the object or another argument of the verb forms a single complex word with the verb – is called noun incorporation.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d39/006.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 6: 8.2.3 Noun Incorporation (p.171)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 6/7</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>8.2.3 Noun Incorporation (p.171)<br>Noun incorporation:<br>- A form of word formation in which a single compound-like word consists of a verb or verb stem and a noun or noun stem that functions as one of its arguments, typically its object.<br>- Noun incorporation tends to occur in languages with polysynthetic morphology.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d39/007.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 7: THE END\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 39 Chapter 8 · slide 7/7</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>THE END<br>THANKS</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
