    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">EMP301 · Chapter 11 · Session 56</span>\n<h2>Session 56 — Chapter 11: Theories of Morphology</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14440 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">EMP301 · Chương 11 · Buổi 56</span>\n<h2>Buổi 56 — Chapter 11: Theories of Morphology</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14440 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO3,5,6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I T U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">6</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO3,5,6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">I T U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">6</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 11: Theories of Morphology<br>Construction Morphology<br>Paradigm Function Morphology</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Course book: Introducing Morphology<br>Chapter 11 (pages 234-239)<br>Online resources</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>Preview the lesson<br>Participate in class discussions and activities<br>Complete tasks before, during, and after the lesson</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>📑 School slides — EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 (6 slides)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">matched by the session number in the deck name. File: EMP301_Session 56_Chapter 11.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>📑 Slide của trường — EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 (6 slide)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">ghép theo số buổi ghi trong tên deck. Tệp: EMP301_Session 56_Chapter 11.pptx</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d53/001.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 1: CHAPTER 11.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 1/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>CHAPTER 11.<br>Theories of Morphology<br>Session 56</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d53/002.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 2: Construction Morphology (CxM), is a branch of a more general theory called Construction Grammar, abbreviated CxG (Booij 2010, 2016…\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 2/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Construction Morphology (CxM), is a branch of a more general theory called Construction Grammar, abbreviated CxG (Booij 2010, 2016; Audring and Masini 2019).<br>﻿Construction Grammar (Goldberg 1995) holds that our mental representations of language are composed of pairings between form and meaning.<br>﻿A grammatical construction is a pattern that imparts meaning apart from the words that make it up. So for example, the verb whistle as we normally use it denotes a certain sort of sound emission (Fenster whistled a catchy tune).<br>﻿11.3 Construction Morphology</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d53/003.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 3: Paradigm Function Morphology (PFM) is used to:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 3/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Paradigm Function Morphology (PFM) is used to:<br>Explains complex inflectional paradigms<br>Focuses on variation across languages<br>Has a strong typological perspective<br>- A lexeme is linked to a set of word forms<br>These forms together create a paradigm<br>Example:<br>walk → walk, walks, walked, walking<br>﻿﻿11.4 Paradigm Function Morphology</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d53/004.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 4: - In PFM, Realization Rules are larger generalizations over Paradigm Functions.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 4/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>- In PFM, Realization Rules are larger generalizations over Paradigm Functions.<br>- ﻿Some Realization Rules are Rules of Exponence, which associate roots that have specific morphosyntactic features with the phonological material that marks those features.<br>﻿﻿11.4 Paradigm Function Morphology</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d53/005.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 5: - The other sort of Realization Rule that PFM makes use of is called a Rule of Referral. Rules of Referral tell us that a word for…\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 5/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>- ﻿The other sort of Realization Rule that PFM makes use of is called a Rule of Referral. Rules of Referral tell us that a word form with one set of morphosyntactic features might systematically be identical to a word form with a different set.<br>﻿﻿11.4 Paradigm Function Morphology</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/EMP301/flm1/d53/006.webp\" alt=\"EMP301 · EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 6: THE END\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"721\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">EMP301 Session 56 Chapter 11 · slide 6/6</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>THE END<br>THANKS</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
